comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T21:01:02.654Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: request-specific all-status linked tracker merge receipt search and full live pm-954h0o and pm-1tns7o lineage plus refreshed strict3116-item corpus and open/in_progress inventories. Existing source-VCS preservation is closed and remains delivered; this is a distinct receipt verification delta. Intake only and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-25T23:41:19.347Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reproduce isolated source/snapshot merge-receipt verification through real Git and preserve durable receipt authority without changing tracker bytes. Bundled with event-read integrity in one reviewed delivery. Only these two implementation items are claimed."
  "2026-10-25T23:57:41.733Z","harness:codex","Real-Git regression passes source and snapshot modes for valid, missing-index and malformed receipts. Child assertions compare copied receipt/history bytes before and after health. Independent same-process controls refuse missing, mismatched or unrelated source coordinates and ignore inherited decoy GIT_DIR/GIT_INDEX_FILE. Snapshot Git objects/index are independent; committed index initialization retains durable authority, including unborn repository handling. Unchanged main fails the positive source-index proof. No source tracker/index/history mutation is performed by verification."
  "2026-10-26T00:40:11.542Z","harness:codex","Additional isolated real-Git acceptance exposed a remaining source/snapshot parity gap before closure: a valid durable receipt staged after the source HEAD is trusted in source mode (1 validated indexed id) but absent from the independent snapshot index (0), because read-tree HEAD preserves only committed entries. The implementation will copy only bounded source-index receipt blobs into the independent snapshot namespace, retaining exact source index evidence for staged and custom tracker roots while preserving missing, conflict-stage, divergent and unrelated proof refusals. No source index or tracker writes are required. This item remains actively claimed; the documented staged-only limitation will be removed with the completed implementation."
  "2026-10-26T00:51:56.011Z","harness:codex","Completed staged/custom-root authority transfer: only bounded stage-zero source-index receipt blobs are written to the independent snapshot object store/index, with the selected tracker rebased into its bound namespace. Inherited default-namespace authority is cleared first. Native Git controls now cover both default and custom tracker roots, staged-only receipts absent from HEAD, untracked copies, conflict stages, divergent working values, and a same-id stale receipt in another committed namespace. Source index/history/receipt bytes remain unchanged. IO controls reject permission faults, missing/broken child input and malformed object identities. Related66-case and63-case focused suites pass; full regression previously passed11432 tests with four remaining branch-coverage edges being completed before the final exact gate."
  "2026-10-26T01:12:51.319Z","harness:codex","Validation: complete quality:static pipeline passed, including exact contracts, dependency/advisory checks, CodeFactor complexity, SDK budgets, tracker assurances and mutation testing. Typecheck passed. Native controls cover source and snapshot authority, staged and custom roots, inherited Git selectors, missing/corrupted proof, sealed timestamps and same-length earlier history changes. Final canonical coverage and packed delivery checks follow before closure."
  "2026-10-26T01:20:20.550Z","harness:codex","Live original snapshot reproduction after exact clone-local command acknowledgment: all ten health assertions pass, including health-integrity-zero=0 and health-history-drift-zero=0. The sole remaining failure is validate-missing-linked-paths=223 against the unchanged source baseline ceiling195. Snapshot excludes the .agents namespace; retained skill/plugin links are a separate path-validation dimension. Preserve this full gate on the existing linked-file hygiene owner; the receipt-specific real-Git suite passes37 tests across7 files. No threshold, history provenance, or project trust policy was changed."
  "2026-10-26T01:39:44.794Z","harness:codex","Final complete source coverage passed: statements71014/71014, branches54642/54642, functions14608/14608, lines67183/67183; zero uncovered counts and no threshold/denominator changes. Full static pipeline, TypeScript targets, linked regressions and9 packed npx/bunx workflows passed. Published2026.10.25 consumer acceptance passed npm and Bun installed-agent sessions plus CLI/MCP transports. Latest pm-changelog is2026.10.25; package-owned regeneration follows closure. Required Sentry/telemetry gate previously passed with0 unresolved issues, fresh pm.command span metadata, exact settled command pairing and drained broker; historical release/nightly limitations remain with canonical owners."
  "2026-10-26T11:37:39.348Z","harness:codex","PR1596 review regression: four real-Git/source faults (corrupt index, missing indexed object, invalid repository metadata, and missing workspace) all silently succeeded before the fix. Snapshot seeding now requests strict source-index reads and aborts before namespace mutation. Native tests compare snapshot index bytes and staged authority, retain the default fail-closed proof-reader contract, and preserve no-Git and no-receipt absence. Non-JSON sidecars no longer trigger unnecessary Git reads. Historical SDK acknowledgement versions are intentionally retained by the surface generator, whose current native check reports zero classified changes."
  "2026-10-26T12:00:52.425Z","harness:codex","Verification audit retained: the full local suite passed11456 tests with3 skips and one failure because this host requires command-local NODE_PATH=<npm module root> to resolve npm/package.json in packed continuation acceptance; that invocation omitted it, so no global coverage report was produced. The concurrent static invocation passed through SDK surface/import-cost checks but its qualified latency gate exceeded unchanged create/claim budgets (428/434ms vs398/415ms). Preserve both failures and verify the affected acceptance with the required environment and latency once without concurrent coverage. Independent native control also found that missing .git/HEAD could fool a diagnostic-based non-Git classifier; that classifier is removed. Snapshot transfer already follows the established Git-identity guard, so strict reads propagate all discovery/index/object errors while outer no-Git snapshots remain supported."
  "2026-10-26T12:03:22.193Z","harness:codex","Final refinement verified: the strict reader propagates every repository discovery/index/object failure and refuses incomplete requested blobs; the shared default reader remains fail closed. Five native fault conditions preserve snapshot index bytes/staged authority. The established outer Git-identity guard retains no-Git snapshot support without diagnostic-text parsing. Final focused30 cases cover both source modules at100/100/100/100 (102 statements,54 branches,14 functions,81 lines); linked44 cases pass. Typecheck/build/ESLint, SDK snapshot, graph/record assurances and mutation testing pass. The isolated unchanged CLI latency gate passes all6 operations; the packed continuation acceptance passes with the host-required npm module-resolution setting. Prior failed concurrent/host invocation evidence remains recorded. Final-head canonical hosted coverage and review remain required for landing."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T01:24:49.550Z","harness:codex","A no-checkout Git clone has no index, and read-tree HEAD omits legitimate staged-only evidence. Snapshot receipt authority must preserve exact bounded stage-zero source-index blobs in its independent object store and selected logical namespace; staging copied working-tree files would manufacture proof."
  "2026-10-26T11:44:01.552Z","harness:codex","Proof evaluation and snapshot setup need distinct read-error policies: durable-proof queries may return no authority on IO failure, but a snapshot transfer must abort before clearing retained authority when its source index or object store cannot be read. Keep legitimate non-Git/empty-index absence separate and prove both policies against native Git failures."
